dent variable is partitioned into the variation explained by the model and the unexplained variation.\n\nThe importance of SS in regression analysis cannot be overstated. It provides a quantitative measure of how well a model explains the variability of the dependent variable, which is essential for model evaluation and selection. By analyzing the proportions of TSS that are attributed to RSS and ESS, researchers can derive the coefficient of determination, \\(R^2\\), which indicates the proportion of variance in the dependent variable that is predictable from the independent variables.\n\nIn summary, the Sum of Squares (SS) is a critical concept in econometrics that quantifies variability in data and is integral to regression analysis. It encompasses the total sum of squares, regression sum of squares, and residual sum of squares, each serving distinct roles in understanding the effectiveness of statistical models. By partitioning total variability into explained and unexplained components, SS aids in evaluating model performance and guiding decision-making in statistical analysis.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "protected_material_code": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "protected_material_text": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}], "created": 1771166092, "model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_f97eff32c5", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 622, "prompt_tokens": 406, "total_tokens": 1028, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0,